Spec: SystemDeleteScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Orchestrate the teardown of one @SystemInstance: run the package's three teardown categories in
    the reverse of the install build-up through @import_run — `delete_pre` hook, `systems`, tofu
    destroy, `crds`, then the `delete_post` hook — and return. This file applies no deletes itself
    and writes nothing: the per-category cluster walks ride the `instance.status` lists install
    recorded, inside the stage modules it dispatches, and zero `status` write, zero
    `set_status_*` call, zero finalizer or CR removal exists here or in the shipped delete stages.
    A clean return only carries the delete Job out of Rust happy-path so the operator releases the
    `systeminstances.vynil.solidite.fr` finalizer (/operator/src/instance_common.sdd
    @run_with_finalizer, @InstanceKind::finalizer_name). Twin notes, real diffs: ./../service/delete.rhai
    is the same skeleton with the single `systems` bucket replaced by five manifest buckets plus a
    `delete_backup` sweep riding the `vitals` gate — two diff hunks separate the files, one before
    the tofu lane and one between tofu and `crds`; ./../tenant/delete.rhai is that file minus
    `crds` and shares nothing further with this shape. This is the only delete lane with no backup
    sweep and the only pure mirror: install here runs `crds → tofu → systems` (./install.rhai),
    delete exactly `systems → tofu → crds` — no tofu position deviation like the service lane.

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`delete.rhai` matches
    @ENTRY_POINT_PATTERNS, `run` is in @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS, /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd);
    invoked as `delete::run(instance, context)` by the fixed snippet of the Rust lane
    /agent/src/system/delete.sdd, whose trailing `;` plus `let _ =` discards the returned value.

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected real @SystemInstance @Dynamic, fetched from the API by the Rust lane
    (whose already-gone-CR hard failure lands before this module is imported). Never read and
    never re-bound here: zero property reads, zero @get_system_instance refresh — install's three
    refreshes have no delete counterpart — only relayed as the first argument to all five
    @import_run calls, so every stage sees the one pre-script `status` snapshot.
  @context — map ./context.rhai's @run lane (./context.sdd) built for this lane. Only key read
    here: `package_dir` — unguarded interpolated property access in all three gate paths (two
    @is_dir, one @has_tofu_files); every other key is consumed by the stage modules, whole maps
    relayed.

Returns:
  No value channel of its own: the implicit value is the trailing `import_run("delete_post", ...)`
    result — the skip `()` on a stock image, the hook ships nowhere — and the caller discards it.
    No observable artifact of its own (no `status` patch, no event, no finalizer touch, no CR
    deletion); observability is the stage-deleted cluster objects and the exit-0/exit-3 outcome
    the clean-return-or-raise produces.

Raises:
  Zero @throw statement in this file: failure is always a propagated engine raise landing in the
    Rust @process::exit(3) lane.
  - Stage/hook module throw: @import_run swallows only the absent-module and absent-`run` markers
    (@log_debug `No ${name} module, skipping.` / `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`, shared
    skip idiom frozen by ./../service/delete.sdd); anything else re-throws and aborts mid-file,
    skipping all later lanes — and no `set_status_*` marker exists on any delete stage (Tasks).
  - @has_tofu_files raise: the tofu gate runs its predicate over an unreadable existing
    `${package_dir}/tofu` past the module-internal @is_dir guard (rules in ./../lib/tofu_gen.sdd).
  - Import-time raise: the top-level `import "tofu_gen" as tfg` pulls `tofu` transitively; an
    unresolvable module in any resolver dir fails the load before @run, packages without `.tf`
    included (import behavior in Must).
  - Property-on-`()` raise after the tofu lane: that lane's guard-free `context = import_run(...)`
    assign lets a shadowed `delete_tofu` without a map-returning `run` leave `context` the `()`
    or a non-map, so the very next gate `${context.package_dir}/crds` raises in interpolation —
    a between-lanes error with a misleading origin (Tasks).

Handles:
  - Category directory absent: the @is_dir gate (`@has_tofu_files` for tofu) skips the whole lane
    — including teardown of its status-recorded entries (status-versus-dir orphan point, Tasks).
    A missing lane module does not raise; it takes the @import_run skip path.
  - Category dir present but nothing installed (`status` `()` — an imported, never-installed CR):
    `delete_systems`/`delete_crds` guard the set-ness of `instance.status` and their category key
    and degrade to hook-noop lanes returning the context; the tofu lane carries no status guard —
    ./delete_tofu.rhai regenerates and destroys over never-installed state, skipping only the
    tfstate restore when @SystemInstance::get_tfstate reads empty (Tasks).
  - `delete_pre`/`delete_post` ship nowhere under ./agent/scripts — on a stock image both take the
    @import_run skip path, return `()` and the @type_of guard sees no map (the hooks exist only as
    package-side scripts under `{package_dir}/scripts`).
  - Context threading: @type_of == `map` merge at `delete_pre`, `delete_systems`, `delete_crds`
    only; `context = import_run("delete_tofu", ...)` is the single guard-free assign; the
    `delete_post` return is discarded. Gate paths are rebuilt from the CURRENT `context`, skipped
    lanes are never revisited and a non-map return is dropped unlogged.

Must:
  Run exactly these lanes, once each, in this order: `import_run("delete_pre", instance, context)`
    with map merge; `is_dir(`${context.package_dir}/systems`)` gate → `delete_systems` with
    merge; `tfg::has_tofu_files(`${context.package_dir}/tofu`)` gate →
    `context = import_run("delete_tofu", instance, context)`, the single guard-free assign;
    `is_dir(`${context.package_dir}/crds`)` gate → `delete_crds` with merge;
    `import_run("delete_post", instance, context)` with no merge and no read of the result — then
    return, nothing after the hook. That order is the exact reverse of ./install.rhai's
    `crds → tofu → systems`: systems first, the whole `crds` group last, tofu the pure mirror.
  Relay @instance unchanged and unread to every lane: no cluster call and no @get_system_instance
    refresh exists at this level (install refreshed because its buckets wrote `status`; the delete
    stages write none), so all five lanes see the one Rust-fetched @SystemInstance.
  Emit no log at this level: install's three @log_info lines have no delete counterpart; every
    observable line comes from the stage modules.
  Load ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai (transitively ./../lib/tofu.rhai) at import time via the single
    top-level import — with the @fn it is the module's only import-time surface.
  Resolve every stage/hook module against the Rust lane's four resolver directories, package
    `scripts` first — the unguarded tofu assign makes a shadowed `delete_tofu` without a
    map-returning `run` a hard raise here (Raises).
  Finish by silence: no `status`/condition/finalizer/CR mutation here or in the shipped stages
    (zero `set_status` occurrences in this directory's `delete_*.rhai`) — success is the clean
    return, completion is the controller releasing `systeminstances.vynil.solidite.fr` after the
    exit-0 Job, failure the raise-to-exit(3) the operator retries with the finalizer held.

Must not:
  Delete from, destroy in or wait inside this file: the `status.systems` two-pass get-delete-wait
    walks, the tfstate restore plus init/destroy and the CRD children-guard all live in the stages
    — importing ./../lib/wait.rhai or calling @delete then @wait_deleted here would duplicate
    lane contracts.
  Gate a rerun skip or a completion on CR state: no read of `status`, conditions or finalizers
    exists here — replays are total, the skip decisions are the three category-directory
    predicates only, and the Rust lane deliberately replays both modules over half-deleted
    instances.

Depends on:
  ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai — the only import; @has_tofu_files answers the `tofu` gate
    (./../lib/tofu_gen.sdd).
  The three shipped stage modules of this directory, all unspecified: ./delete_systems.rhai —
    two-pass teardown ordering the tail list (Service, Deployment, ServiceAccount, ClusterRole,
    ClusterRoleBinding, Role, RoleBinding, Secret, ConfigMap, PersistentVolume,
    PersistentVolumeClaim, Namespace) last and everything else first, each pass an
    api-existence, NotFound-tolerant get-delete walk then a 300 s wait of the deleted objects,
    wrapped by `delete_systems_pre`/`_post`; ./delete_tofu.rhai — byte-identical to
    ./../service/delete_tofu.rhai: restore @SystemInstance::get_tfstate, `tfg::gen_files`, the
    ./../lib/tofu.rhai init+destroy lane; ./delete_crds.rhai — byte-identical to
    ./../service/delete_crds.rhai: delete recorded CRDs, warn-skip kinds that still list
    children. Roles quoted only; their contracts are theirs.
  wynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — the 3-arg @import_run global shim injected by @Script @add_common
    (the skip-vs-rethrow boundary quoted in Raises), @is_dir, @type_of; mounted by the
    constructor of /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd.
  ./context.rhai (./context.sdd) + ./../lib/build_context.rhai — producer of every `context` key;
    key contract owned by ./../lib/build_context.sdd, kind slot ./context_system.rhai
    (./context_system.sdd).

References:
  /agent/src/system/delete.sdd — the caller: snippet, `instance`/`args` injection, resolver dirs,
    the already-gone-CR hard failure landing before this module runs, and the exit-3 error lane
    all raises here land in.
  ./../service/delete.sdd — calibration sibling freezing the shared hook/merge idiom, the
    skip-marker quotes and the unguarded-tofu open point.
  ./../tenant/delete.rhai (./../tenant/delete.sdd) — service minus `crds`; the three delete lanes
    share the skeleton and differ in bucket sets only.
  /operator/src/instance_common.sdd — the other half of finalization: @run_with_finalizer removes
    the kind finalizer only after the delete Job answers clean; a raise here holds it.
  ./install.rhai (./install.sdd) — the install twin whose bucket order this file mirrors exactly.
  ./../lib/wait.sdd — owner of the @wait_deleted posture the stages reuse untouched here.
  /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs — harness with zero system-lane cases (Tasks).

Scenario: full three-category order with directories present
  Given a package dir holding `systems`, `crds` and user `.tf` sources, on a live engine with the
    three shipped stages resolvable
  When @run executes
  Then the modules are imported in exactly pre → systems → tofu → crds → post order, the two
    is_dir buckets merging only a map return and tofu assigning its return unguarded
  And @instance is passed through unchanged — no refresh here, every stage reads the pre-script
    @SystemInstance snapshot
  No mapped test: the harness carries no system delete case.

Scenario: stock image and empty package skip clean
  Given a stock image (the `delete_pre`/`delete_post` pair ships nowhere) on a package dir with
    no `systems`, no `crds` and no user `.tf` file
  When @run executes
  Then both hooks and all three gates take the @import_run/@is_dir/@has_tofu_files skip paths
    with debug logs only, and @run returns the hook-skip value error-free
  No mapped test.

Scenario: never-installed instance runs lanes without deleting
  Given a package whose `systems` and `crds` dirs are present but a CR whose `status` is empty
    (imported, never installed)
  When @run reaches a taken gate and its stage module runs
  Then the systems/crds set-ness guards short-circuit their delete loops — hooks-only no-op
    lanes, context returned, nothing deleted, no raise
  But the tofu lane still resolves — it carries no status guard — skipping only the tfstate
    restore because the state reads empty (Tasks)
  No mapped test.

Scenario: tofu context clobber kills the next gate
  Given a package shadowing `delete_tofu` with a module whose `run` is missing or returns a
    non-map, and a true tofu gate
  When @run reaches the tofu exit
  Then `context` becomes `()` (or the non-map) — the assignment carries no @type_of guard — and
    the `${context.package_dir}/crds` gate interpolation raises, aborting the delete with an
    error originating between lanes, not inside any stage
  The shipped ./delete_tofu.rhai always returns the context map; recorded behavior, see Tasks,
    no mapped test.

Scenario: stage throw aborts with no delete-side marker
  Given a stage that fails — a @wait_deleted timeout in ./delete_systems.rhai, a destroy raise
    from ./delete_tofu.rhai, or any non-skip error re-thrown by a stage
  When the throw crosses @import_run
  Then it is not one of the two skip markers, so it re-throws: no later category, no
    `delete_post`, and no `set_status_*` failure write exists anywhere on this lane to record it
    — the Rust lane fails to @process::exit(3) and the controller keeps the
    `systeminstances.vynil.solidite.fr` finalizer for a retried Job
  No mapped test.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenarios to /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs: no system-lane test exists (its
      resolver dirs ship `scripts/service` and `scripts/lib` only); add a `scripts/system` entry,
      a fixture package with `systems`/`crds`/`.tf` and mock stage modules to pin the five-call
      order, the three gate predicates, the merge posture and the throw-abort on the mock engine.
  [ ] Author the three pending stage specs quoted under `Depends on`; their quoted roles
      (two-pass kind ordering, 300 s waits, tfstate restore, children-guard skip) must be verified
      there, not restated.
  [?] Bucket skipping is directory-based, status-blind: `status.systems`/`status.crds` entries
      whose directory is absent at delete time are never deleted, yet the run returns clean and
      the controller releases the finalizer — recorded resources orphan silently. Decide whether
      a non-empty status bucket must force its lane regardless of the directory.
  [?] Unguarded tofu return (Scenario "tofu context clobber"): a package-shaped `delete_tofu`
      turns the whole delete into a property-on-`()` raise at the `crds` gate with a misleading
      origin. ./../service/delete.sdd holds the identical open point on the same line; decide one
      guarded pattern for both kinds' lanes together.
  [?] The tofu lane runs with no status guard: an imported-but-never-installed instance with user
      `.tf` sources still gets gen_files + init + destroy (only the tfstate restore is
      state-conditional). Confirm destroying empty state is intended, or gate the lane on a
      stored `status.tfstate`.
  [?] `delete_post` return is discarded while `delete_pre` merges — nothing runs after the post
      hook, so that merge feeds no consumer; the service twin carries the same asymmetry. Decide
      whether the hook pair should share one merge posture.
  [?] A stage raise leaves the delete lane with no CR-visible trace (no failure condition, no
      event): only the held finalizer and the Job's exit 3 drive the retry while `status` keeps
      telling the install-time story. Confirm the markerless delete posture is intended.

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mapped test or a recorded decision, the five-call order and
    gate texts above still match the source, the three stage specs exist, and `specdd lint` is
    green on this file.
